\/future-programming-languages\/#faq-question-1784610816459","position":10,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-programming-languages\/#faq-question-1784610816459","name":"10. Are C and C++ still relevant for the future?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, C and C++ remain highly relevant for system programming, game development, embedded systems, and performance critical applications. Their control over hardware keeps them in steady demand.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-programming-languages\/#faq-question-1784610835681","position":11,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/future-programming-languages\/#faq-question-1784610835681","name":"11. Which future coding language is best for mobile app development?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kotlin and Java are best for native Android apps, while Swift is the top choice for iOS. For cross platform apps, languages that pair with frameworks like Flutter and React Native are also popular.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"}]}},"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12646","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/13"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=12646"}],"version-history":[{"count":17,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12646\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":22959,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12646\/revisions\/22959"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog